mailove (3.7.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Bulk sending, off by default: with compose/bulkSend set in the
    advanced settings a Bulk checkbox appears in the composer. Checked,
    the To field becomes a list (one address per line, or separated by
    commas), Cc/Bcc go away, and Send becomes hold-to-send
    (compose/bulkHoldSecs). Every address gets its own message with its
    own To header and Message-ID, encrypted to that one recipient when
    encryption is on; attachments are carried by each.
  * The batch goes through the Outbox on a connection of its own, so it
    keeps sending while you read mail in another account, at
    compose/bulkDelayMs between messages. A lost connection or an expired
    sign-in pauses it and it reconnects by itself; a rejected address
    fails only that row. Progress (n of total, the address on the wire,
    failures) sits in the top bar with a Cancel that drops what has not
    gone out. Each message's Sent copy is optional (compose/bulkSentCopy).
  * A dismissed passphrase prompt during a bulk send cancels the whole
    send with nothing queued, instead of asking once per recipient and
    sending unsigned.
  * Links in the composer: a typed web or mail address becomes a link
    when the space or line break after it is typed. Ctrl+K (or the link
    button) opens a dialog with the link text and its target as separate
    fields, edits the link under the cursor whole, and can remove it.
  * The advanced settings are readable from QML (Advanced.get), for
    features whose switches live only there.
  * When the GUI thread stalls for more than two seconds a backtrace of
    it is sampled and logged under the "stalled" line (mailove.trace),
    so a freeze can be located rather than only measured.

 -- dusoft <dusoft@bastadigital.com>  Wed, 30 Sep 2026 12:00:00 +0200

mailove (3.6.2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * The RPM installed on Fedora and openSUSE but would not start:
    "version `Qt_6_PRIVATE_API' not found". The QML compiler pulled in
    two Qt private symbols whose version those distributions rename per
    Qt release. QML is now compiled to bytecode only; the binary has no
    private Qt imports left (GitHub #5).
  * Gmail set up as a plain IMAP account with the normal Google password
    fails to log in once 2-Step Verification is on, and the server's
    reply was elided to "Application specif..." in the status bar. The
    login error now says what to do (use the Gmail / Google Workspace
    account type, or an app password), and the account sheet says the
    same when the IMAP server is a Gmail one (GitHub #5).
  * A Gmail or Microsoft account signed in with its own or the advanced
    settings' client pair was skipped by every background poll, so its
    unread count never updated while another account was open. The poll
    resolves the client pair the same way the foreground does; a skipped
    account is now logged with the reason.
  * New arrivals in a background account that were spam candidates
    pending their body are remembered per account, so they are still
    filed when that account is opened instead of being forgotten.
  * The AppImage no longer logs "Failed to register with host portal …
    App info not found" on every launch: it announces the desktop entry
    AppImageLauncher wrote if there is one, and none otherwise.

 -- dusoft <dusoft@bastadigital.com>  Sat, 27 Sep 2026 12:00:00 +0200

mailove (3.6.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * A reply-all that copies your own address is no longer marked as spam.
    Your server records such mail as an authenticated submission
    (auth=pass) and grades nothing else, which the scorer read as
    "nothing vouches for it" and scored +100. auth=pass now exempts mail
    from your own address; it is never a pass for anyone else's.
    New switch spam/trustAuth in advanced.conf.
  * The "delivered in one hop from a machine with no host name" rule no
    longer fires on your own server's submission line (with ESMTPSA).
  * Without a Public Suffix List (first run before the download lands,
    or offline) the scorer compared full host names, so a shop's link
    reading "packeta.sk" and going to www.packeta.sk scored a mismatch.
    The fallback now errs the other way and can only under-report.
  * A new arrival opened before the prefetch reached it was marked as
    spam by the body rules but left in the inbox; it is filed now, like
    any other arrival. Mail already in the inbox is still never moved.
  * The reading pane occasionally showed the older message one row down
    under a newly arrived one until the folder was reopened: a body
    fetched for a message you had already left was still presented over
    the one you moved to. Such answers are cached and no longer shown,
    and a failed fetch for a message you left no longer blanks the pane.
  * Clicking the status line opens the activity log on that message;
    every status crumb is logged (mailove.status).
  * Copying from the activity log yields a fenced code block, so it
    pastes as a log into a bug tracker or chat rather than as prose.

 -- dusoft <dusoft@bastadigital.com>  Wed, 16 Sep 2026 16:00:00 +0200

